<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter Kropotkin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1842">1842</a>–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Pyotr Alexeyevich Kropotkin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter Kropotkin was a Russian anarchist political philosopher and geographer, a proponent of anarchist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communism">communism</a>. Born into an aristocratic land-owning family, he attended the Page Corps and served as an officer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>, where he took part in geological expeditions. Imprisoned for his activism in 1874, he escaped two years later and spent 41 years in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. He argued for a decentralised communist society of voluntary associations of self-governing communities and worker-run enterprises, in The Conquest of Bread (1892) and Mutual Aid: A Factor of Evolution (1902). He returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1917 but was disappointed by the Bolshevik state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-kropotkin.jpg" alt="Peter Kropotkin" width="330" height="475" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nadar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Kropotkin_circa_1900.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Proudhon’s mutualism called for free contract, federation and a bank of the people; Bakunin’s collectivism for collective ownership and pay by time worked; <b>Kropotkin</b>’s anarcho-communism for distribution according to need; anarcho-syndicalism for unions of workers to run society.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/anarchism">Anarchism · Core Ideas</a></li><li><blockquote>Leninists rely on a vanguard party of professional revolutionaries bound by democratic centralism; libertarian communists favour workers’ councils and self-management; anarcho-communists such as <b>Peter Kropotkin</b> wanted society to pass at once to communism, without a state.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/communism">Communism · Core Ideas</a></li></ul></section>
